{
  "raw": {
    "https://talentandculture.wvu.edu/employee-relations/required-postings": {
      "title": "Required Postings",
      "description": "Required Postings | Talent and Culture | West Virginia University Skip to main content Talent and Culture Careers WVU Home Search Would you like to search this site specifically, or all WVU websites? Search this site Search WVU Toggle Search Benefits and Compensation Benefits Strategy Compensation Learning and Organizational Development Course Catalog Programs and Workshops Appreciation and Recognition Our Team Employee Relations Medical Management Handbooks Required Postings Conflict Resolution Resources Discipline Filing a Grievance Equal Opportunity Fitness for Duty Guidelines Employee Code of Conduct Unemployment Compensation Flexible Work Arrangements Strategic HR Partners Strategic HR Partners Directory Performance Management New Employees New Mountaineer Orientation Policies, Forms and Resources Supervisor/EBO FMLA Responsibility Hiring Resources Employee Offboarding Process Home Employee Relations Required Postings Required Postings Listed below are employee notices you should be aware of and read carefully. These\n  notices are posted at various locations around campus. Many of our Talent and Culture\n  policies and procedures reflect the requirements outlined in these notices. These notices explain employee rights about topics such as equal employment opportunity\n  (EEO), family and medical leave (FMLA), unemployment compensation, workers’ compensation,\n  human rights and the rights of employees who are in the armed services, among\n  others. Equal Employment Opportunity Family and Medical Leave Act OSHA Job Safety and Health Parental Leave Act Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision USERRA - The Uniformed Services Employment and Reemployment Rights Act Workers' Compensation Workforce West Virginia - Unemployment Benefits WV Human Rights Act Employee Rights Under the Fair Labor Standards Act WV Minimum Wage Requirements WV Wage Payment & Collection Act WV Whistle Blower Law WVU EthicsLine WVU Online Raffle License Medical Management Handbooks Required Postings Conflict Resolution Resources Discipline Filing a Grievance Equal Opportunity Fitness for Duty Guidelines Employee Code of Conduct Unemployment Compensation Flexible Work Arrangements Contact us Talent and Culture Location: - 4 8 Donley Street - 4th Fl, Morgantown, WV 26501 Phone: 304-293-5700 Fax: 304-293-7532 Email: TalentandCulture@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Operating Hours 8:15 a.m. to 4:45 p.m. Monday - Friday Excluding University holidays Equal Opportunity University Holidays Event Calendar Retirees Association Staff Council Accreditations Web Standards Privacy Notice Questions or Comments? © 2026 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on March 16, 2026. A-Z Site Index Campus Map WVU Careers Directory Give Handshake WVU Safety Notification System WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"
    },
    "https://careers.wvu.edu/career-opportunities": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities",
      "description": "Career Opportunities | Careers | West Virginia University Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Search Would you like to search this site specifically, or all WVU websites? Search this site Search WVU Toggle Search Home Career Opportunities Why WVU WVU Achievements and Rankings Outdoor Adventure Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Community Info Dual Career Program Required Notices Home Career Opportunities Career Opportunities Want to go beyond in your career? Explore open positions at WVU. WVU Faculty WVU students are our top priority, and serving them starts with you. Our professors\n  and instructors are equipped with top-tier facilities and resources so they can\n  provide a high-quality education and produce world changing research. View Faculty Positions WVU Staff From accountants and researchers to electricians and IT specialists, the WVU campus\n  is like a small city. Find your fit in a unique academic setting. View Staff Portal WVU Temporary WVU offers temporary employment to those starting out in their careers or looking\n  for a change. Temporary positions exist across the Morgantown campus in all types\n  of roles. View Temporary Positions Or learn about the Temporary Employment Program . WVU HAS IMMEDIATE OPENINGS IN UNIVERSITY POLICE. University Police offers: $22 starting hourly rate. Incremental hourly raises tied to milestones in the training program. Full-time, benefits-eligible positions. Part-time positions if West Virginia Law Enforcement Certified. Overtime opportunities. Eligibility for three retention incentives starting second year. View current opportunities DUAL CAREER PROGRAM Finding a job for yourself is one thing. Finding a job for you and your spouse or partner\n  is another challenge. We support professional couples. At WVU, we understand that meeting the needs of professional couples is critical\n  to recruiting and retaining faculty, staff and physicians. Many candidates and\n  newly hired employees have spouses or partners who also are seeking employment\n  at the University or in the Morgantown area – the Dual Career Program helps with\n  their career transition and job search. Learn more about the WVU Dual Career program applicant resources Have a question about applying? We have answers. How to apply Find answers to the most frequently asked questions about applying for a position with WVU and using the WVUHire application system. Learn how to apply Request Accommodations WVU's commitment to excellence is the force that drives our hiring decisions, and we welcome applications from all job seekers. Learn how to request accommodations Hints and Tips Find advice on the WVU application process, from writing your resume to acing your interview. Get tips on the application process Still need help? Contact the Shared Services Center at 304-293-6006. Contact Us Talent Acquisition and Recruitment Location : 4 8 Donely Street, 4th Fl, Morgantown, WV  26501 Phone : 304-293-6006 Email : Employment@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Operating Hours 8:15 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Monday - Friday Excluding University holidays Announcements No announcements to show. Accreditations Web Standards Privacy Notice Questions or Comments? © 2026 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on July 24, 2025. A-Z Site Index Campus Map WVU Careers Directory Give Handshake WVU Safety Notification System WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"
    },
    "https://careers.wvu.edu/why-wvu": {
      "title": "Why WVU",
      "description": "Why WVU | Careers | West Virginia University Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Search Would you like to search this site specifically, or all WVU websites? Search this site Search WVU Toggle Search Home Career Opportunities Why WVU WVU Achievements and Rankings Outdoor Adventure Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Community Info Dual Career Program Required Notices Home Why WVU Why WVU we love the old gold and blue Discover what it means to be a Mountaineer. At WVU, we pride ourselves on a tireless endeavor for achievement.\n  We are home to some of the most passionate, innovative minds in the country who go beyond for the sake of progress, constantly moving the world forward. Through our shared values, WVU students, faculty and staff make this institution one of the best out there. We are proud to stand as one voice, one University, one WVU. Learn how you can join the Mountaineer family live like a Mountaineer At WVU, we believe that finding the right fit is the key to success. Mission, Vision and Values Being a Mountaineer means you have a passion for our values: service, curiosity, respect, accountability and appreciation. Learn about our mission “I truly believe in the work that I do and that it positively impacts the environment and lives of West Virginians. Working at WVU makes me feel like I’m a part of something far bigger than myself.” — Stephanie Toothman, Office of Sustainability “West Virginia has become a home for me. I was able to achieve most of the things I wanted in my career, with a nice balance between work and life.” — Dr. Mohamad Salkini, Division of Urologic Oncology “The research community here has been very supportive. The mentoring environment is superb for junior faculty and I am nurtured in\n  an environment that is conducive to my success.” — Dr. Candice Brown, Dept. of Microbiology, Immunology and Cell Biology find out for yourself Hear what employees in WVU Facilities and Services have to say about working at the University. Want to know more about what it's like to work for WVU? Hear about it from some of our employees! You'll get a look at some of the types of careers we offer and the benefits of being a Mountaineer. your total rewards Discover the benefits of being a Mountaineer. Benefits and Compensation Mountaineers take care of each other. View health insurance, compensation, wellness opportunities and more. View our benefits options Wellness and Perks We believe in working smart and playing smart. See the fun side of a successful career with WVU. View Mountaineer perks EXPLORE FACULTY RESOURCES As an R1 institution, WVU faculty members have access to top resources and facilities. View faculty information Multiple campuses, 1 great fit WVU is a family of distinctive campuses united by a single goal: to provide a quality education. Find the campus that's right for you. Learn more about our campuses Contact Us Talent Acquisition and Recruitment Location : 4 8 Donely Street, 4th Fl, Morgantown, WV  26501 Phone : 304-293-6006 Email : Employment@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Operating Hours 8:15 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Monday - Friday Excluding University holidays Announcements No announcements to show. Accreditations Web Standards Privacy Notice Questions or Comments? © 2026 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on February 20, 2025. A-Z Site Index Campus Map WVU Careers Directory Give Handshake WVU Safety Notification System WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"
    },
    "https://careers.wvu.edu/outdoor-adventure/biking": {
      "title": "Biking",
      "description": "Biking | Careers | West Virginia University Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Search Would you like to search this site specifically, or all WVU websites? Search this site Search WVU Toggle Search Home Career Opportunities Why WVU WVU Achievements and Rankings Outdoor Adventure Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Community Info Dual Career Program Required Notices Home Outdoor Adventure Biking Biking Whether it's for relaxation or exhilaration, get on your bike and enjoy the ride. In 2019, WVU was named a bronze-level Bicycle-Friendly University SM by the League of American Bicyclists . The City of Morgantown also was named a bronze-level\n  Bicycle-Friendly Community SM . WVU is among 208 colleges and universities in 47 states and the District of Columbia\n    that received the bicycle-friendly designation, and the University is the only\n    academic institution in West Virginia to be recognized. Beyond our campus, the Rail-Trail is a great way to explore Morgantown and the surrounding area\n    by bike. And our state is home to several exciting and family-friendly mountain\n    biking trails—from beginning and intermediate levels to advanced levels. Learn more about biking in the Mountain State Visit the West Virginia Tourism Office website Explore our interactive map Outdoor Adventure Opportunities Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Additional Resources WVU DIY Outdoors West Virginia Tourism Office Contact Us Talent Acquisition and Recruitment Location : 4 8 Donely Street, 4th Fl, Morgantown, WV  26501 Phone : 304-293-6006 Email : Employment@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Operating Hours 8:15 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Monday - Friday Excluding University holidays Announcements No announcements to show. Accreditations Web Standards Privacy Notice Questions or Comments? © 2026 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on August 13, 2024. A-Z Site Index Campus Map WVU Careers Directory Give Handshake WVU Safety Notification System WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"
    },
    "https://careers.wvu.edu/outdoor-adventure/climbing": {
      "title": "Climbing",
      "description": "Climbing | Careers | West Virginia University Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Search Would you like to search this site specifically, or all WVU websites? Search this site Search WVU Toggle Search Home Career Opportunities Why WVU WVU Achievements and Rankings Outdoor Adventure Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Community Info Dual Career Program Required Notices Home Outdoor Adventure Climbing Climbing This is why we call ourselves Mountaineers. West Virginia boasts some of the best sport climbing, bouldering, single and multi-pitch\n    trad climbing in the eastern U.S. From Seneca Rocks featuring craggy and airy peaks, to the New River\n    Gorge with more than 3,000 routes featuring smooth cliffs along a deep\n    river canyon, West Virginia’s climbing areas offer unrivaled scenery and\n    are accessible to climbers at all levels. Learn more about climbing in the Mountain State Visit the West Virginia Tourism Office website Explore our interactive map Outdoor Adventure Opportunities Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Additional Resources WVU DIY Outdoors West Virginia Tourism Office Contact Us Talent Acquisition and Recruitment Location : 4 8 Donely Street, 4th Fl, Morgantown, WV  26501 Phone : 304-293-6006 Email : Employment@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Operating Hours 8:15 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Monday - Friday Excluding University holidays Announcements No announcements to show. Accreditations Web Standards Privacy Notice Questions or Comments? © 2026 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on August 13, 2024. A-Z Site Index Campus Map WVU Careers Directory Give Handshake WVU Safety Notification System WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"
    },
    "https://careers.wvu.edu/outdoor-adventure/hiking": {
      "title": "Hiking",
      "description": "Hiking | Careers | West Virginia University Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Search Would you like to search this site specifically, or all WVU websites? Search this site Search WVU Toggle Search Home Career Opportunities Why WVU WVU Achievements and Rankings Outdoor Adventure Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Community Info Dual Career Program Required Notices Home Outdoor Adventure Hiking Hiking These views are worth the trek. West Virginia’s topography is vast and varied. Our trails extend across steep mountaintops\n    and winding valleys and offer trekkers a wide range of hiking opportunities—from family-friendly paths to overnight trails. But regardless of your interest or skill level, all of our trails offer amazing\n    views. In fact, after taking in the scenery from one of our trails, you will\n    understand why West Virginia is known as ‘Almost Heaven.’ Learn more about hiking in West Virginia Visit the West Virginia Tourism Office website Explore our interactive map Outdoor Adventure Opportunities Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Additional Resources WVU DIY Outdoors West Virginia Tourism Office Contact Us Talent Acquisition and Recruitment Location : 4 8 Donely Street, 4th Fl, Morgantown, WV  26501 Phone : 304-293-6006 Email : Employment@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Operating Hours 8:15 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Monday - Friday Excluding University holidays Announcements No announcements to show. Accreditations Web Standards Privacy Notice Questions or Comments? © 2026 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on August 14, 2024. A-Z Site Index Campus Map WVU Careers Directory Give Handshake WVU Safety Notification System WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"
    },
    "https://careers.wvu.edu/outdoor-adventure/kayaking": {
      "title": "Kayaking",
      "description": "Kayaking | Careers | West Virginia University Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Search Would you like to search this site specifically, or all WVU websites? Search this site Search WVU Toggle Search Home Career Opportunities Why WVU WVU Achievements and Rankings Outdoor Adventure Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Community Info Dual Career Program Required Notices Home Outdoor Adventure Kayaking Kayaking This is how we 'roll' in West Virginia. West Virginia offers kayakers and paddlers the opportunity to explore more than\n    24,000 square miles of rivers amidst some of America's most scenic countryside.\n    And our rivers offer everything from tranquil waters to big waves, swirling hydraulics\n    and sweeping waterfalls. Kayaking and canoeing options across the state are available for the beginner through\n    the experienced paddler. Opportunities exist for paddling and fishing, paddling\n    to spots where you can rock climb right out of the water or go on multi-day river\n    trips. Learn more about kayaking and paddling in the Mountain State Visit the West Virginia Tourism Office website Explore our interactive map Outdoor Adventure Opportunities Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Additional Resources WVU DIY Outdoors West Virginia Tourism Office Contact Us Talent Acquisition and Recruitment Location : 4 8 Donely Street, 4th Fl, Morgantown, WV  26501 Phone : 304-293-6006 Email : Employment@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Operating Hours 8:15 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Monday - Friday Excluding University holidays Announcements No announcements to show. Accreditations Web Standards Privacy Notice Questions or Comments? © 2026 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on August 14, 2024. A-Z Site Index Campus Map WVU Careers Directory Give Handshake WVU Safety Notification System WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"
    },
    "https://careers.wvu.edu/outdoor-adventure/rafting": {
      "title": "Rafting",
      "description": "Rafting | Careers | West Virginia University Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Search Would you like to search this site specifically, or all WVU websites? Search this site Search WVU Toggle Search Home Career Opportunities Why WVU WVU Achievements and Rankings Outdoor Adventure Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Community Info Dual Career Program Required Notices Home Outdoor Adventure Rafting Rafting Sometimes it's better to go with the flow. West Virginia is recognized around the globe for its stellar whitewater rafting.\n    And the Mountain State offers something for every kind of rafting enthusiast—from beginners to experts. From tranquil float trips on the Lower New River to intense multi-class rapids\n    on the Upper Gauley River, West Virginia is whitewater rafting at its very best.\n    And located just outside of Morgantown, the Cheat River boasts 13 miles of whitewater\n    adventure amidst some of West Virginia’s most breathtaking scenery. Learn more about whitewater rafting in the Mountain State Visit the West Virginia Tourism Office website Explore our interactive map Outdoor Adventure Opportunities Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Additional Resources WVU DIY Outdoors West Virginia Tourism Office Contact Us Talent Acquisition and Recruitment Location : 4 8 Donely Street, 4th Fl, Morgantown, WV  26501 Phone : 304-293-6006 Email : Employment@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Operating Hours 8:15 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Monday - Friday Excluding University holidays Announcements No announcements to show. Accreditations Web Standards Privacy Notice Questions or Comments? © 2026 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on August 14, 2024. A-Z Site Index Campus Map WVU Careers Directory Give Handshake WVU Safety Notification System WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"
    },
    "https://careers.wvu.edu/outdoor-adventure/skiing": {
      "title": "Skiing",
      "description": "Skiing | Careers | West Virginia University Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Search Would you like to search this site specifically, or all WVU websites? Search this site Search WVU Toggle Search Home Career Opportunities Why WVU WVU Achievements and Rankings Outdoor Adventure Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Community Info Dual Career Program Required Notices Home Outdoor Adventure Skiing Skiing The mountains are calling, and you must go. With several cross-country locations and major ski resorts across the state, West Virginia\n  offers some of the best skiing in the Mid-Atlantic region. Our ski resorts include: Snowshoe Mountain Resort (Pocahontas County, West Virginia) Located about two and a half hours from Morgantown near Washington, D.C.,\n    Snowshoe is home to 257 acres of skiable terrain, 1500 vertical feet, 60\n    trails and some of the best snow around. The Village of Snowshoe features several options for eating, shopping and lodging. Canaan Valley Resort (Tucker County, West Virginia) Located two hours from Morgantown in Canaan Valley State Park, Canaan Valley\n      Resort receives approximately 180 inches of snowfall annually. Catering to\n      skiers and snowboarders alike, Canaan Valley Resort offers 47 trails that range\n      from beginner to advanced levels. The resort also offers a family-friendly\n      1,200-foot snow tubing park. Winterplace (Raleigh County, West Virginia) Located three hours from Morgantown and just five minutes off I-77, Exit 28,\n      Winterplace offers 27 trails and a terrain park on 90 acres of skiable terrain.\n      All runs have 100% snowmaking capabilities. Winterplace also offers West\n      Virginia's largest snow tubing park. Learn more about skiing in West Virginia Visit the West Virginia Tourism Office website Explore our interactive map Outdoor Adventure Opportunities Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Additional Resources WVU DIY Outdoors West Virginia Tourism Office Contact Us Talent Acquisition and Recruitment Location : 4 8 Donely Street, 4th Fl, Morgantown, WV  26501 Phone : 304-293-6006 Email : Employment@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Operating Hours 8:15 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Monday - Friday Excluding University holidays Announcements No announcements to show. Accreditations Web Standards Privacy Notice Questions or Comments? © 2026 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on August 14, 2024. A-Z Site Index Campus Map WVU Careers Directory Give Handshake WVU Safety Notification System WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"
    },
    "https://careers.wvu.edu/community-information": {
      "title": "Love West Virginia.LIVE West Virginia.",
      "description": "Community Info | Careers | West Virginia University Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Search Would you like to search this site specifically, or all WVU websites? Search this site Search WVU Toggle Search Home Career Opportunities Why WVU WVU Achievements and Rankings Outdoor Adventure Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Community Info Dual Career Program Required Notices Love West Virginia. LIVE West Virginia. WVU is a family of distinctive campuses united by a single goal: to provide a quality\n  education. We have campuses in Morgantown, Keyser and Beckley and Extension Offices\n  in all 55 West Virginia counties. The WVU Health Sciences Center also has campuses\n  in Morgantown, Charleston and Martinsburg. WVU Beckley WVU Tech, located on the WVU Beckley campus, offers competitive engineering programs\n  and a variety of other challenging majors to its more than 1,300 students. Enrollment 1,347 Academics 40+ bachelor degree programs 12:1 student-faculty ratio Average class size: 17 All courses taught by faculty Location Beckley, population 17,238 (West Virginia’s 9th largest city), in southern West Virginia Learn more about WVU Beckley WVU Morgantown In Morgantown, West Virginia University is home to over 28,400 students. You’ll find\n  groundbreaking research, trailblazing spirit and endless academic opportunities. Enrollment 28,488 Academics 341 majors leading to undergraduate, graduate and professional degrees 21:1 student-faculty ratio Courses taught by faculty and graduate students Location Morgantown, population 31,073 (West Virginia’s 3rd largest city), in the north-central\n  region of the state bordering Pennsylvania and Maryland. Morgantown was ranked\n  number 16 on Business Insider's list of Best College Towns. Learn more about WVU Morgantown WVU Keyser Potomac State College, located on the WVU Keyser campus, is known for its small size\n  and tradition of academic excellence – for nearly 1,500 students, we are a home\n  away from home. And our tuition remains one of the lowest in the state for a four-year\n  institution. Enrollment 1,452 Academics Two- and four-year degrees, including 50+ associate and four bachelor’s programs 20:1 student-faculty ratio Average class size: 22 All courses taught by faculty Location Keyser, population 5,264, in West Virginia’s eastern panhandle bordering Maryland Learn more about WVU Keyser Contact Us Talent Acquisition and Recruitment Location : 4 8 Donely Street, 4th Fl, Morgantown, WV  26501 Phone : 304-293-6006 Email : Employment@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Operating Hours 8:15 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Monday - Friday Excluding University holidays Announcements No announcements to show. Accreditations Web Standards Privacy Notice Questions or Comments? © 2026 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on February 25, 2021. A-Z Site Index Campus Map WVU Careers Directory Give Handshake WVU Safety Notification System WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"
    },
    "https://careers.wvu.edu/career-opportunities/dual-career-program": {
      "title": "Dual Career Program",
      "description": "Dual Career Program | Careers | West Virginia University Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Search Would you like to search this site specifically, or all WVU websites? Search this site Search WVU Toggle Search Home Career Opportunities Why WVU WVU Achievements and Rankings Outdoor Adventure Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Community Info Dual Career Program Required Notices Home Career Opportunities Dual Career Program Dual Career Program Our Mission Attract and retain dual career couples to WVU and Morgantown, West Virginia Enrich WVU’s commitment to talent retention Provide customized assistance and support to clients in their job search efforts Engage employers to build networks for possible client referrals and employment\n      opportunities Program Services The Dual Career Program assists with: Career consulting and job search assistance. Client referrals to hiring managers, when appropriate. Employment resources and networking opportunities. Résumé writing, cover letters and interviewing techniques. Information on open positions at WVU and job postings for local employers, as well\n    as general community and relocation information. The Dual Career Program is also proud to assist WVU Veteran employee spouses in\n    their job searches. Although there is no guarantee of job placement, the Dual Career Program will help\n  with job searches for an employee’s spouse or partner through professional networking\n  and employment referrals – for both WVU and the Morgantown area. To participate in the Dual Career Program, you should be: The spouse/partner of a newly hired, full-time, benefits-eligible WVU faculty member,\n    staff employee or physician AND have lived in the area for fewer than 12 months. The spouse/partner of a current full-time, benefits-eligible faculty member or\n    staff employee with a written request submitted directly by the employee’s vice\n    president, dean or department chair. program resources Find out all the information you need as a potential Dual Career client. Eligibility Requirements The Dual Career Program is designed to help spouses/partners of newly hired WVU employees who are relocating to Morgantown. Find Out if You Are Eligible Frequently Asked Questions Get information on all of the most important topics related to our program. View the FAQs Career Resources Check out this list of local universities, state employment resources and regional Chamber of Commerce listings. View Career Resources Request a Consultation Interested in discussing your employment goals? Complete the Consultation Request Form find out more Reach out to our Dual Career Coordinator to get more information. Get in touch with our Dual Career Coordinator any time to discuss your interest in the Program or to find out more information. Contact the Dual Career Coordinator at: DualCareer@mail.wvu.edu Contact Us Talent Acquisition and Recruitment Location : 4 8 Donely Street, 4th Fl, Morgantown, WV  26501 Phone : 304-293-6006 Email : Employment@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Operating Hours 8:15 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Monday - Friday Excluding University holidays Announcements No announcements to show. Accreditations Web Standards Privacy Notice Questions or Comments? © 2026 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on February 20, 2025. A-Z Site Index Campus Map WVU Careers Directory Give Handshake WVU Safety Notification System WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"
    },
    "https://careers.wvu.edu/required-notices": {
      "title": "Required Notices",
      "description": "Required Notices | Careers | West Virginia University Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Search Would you like to search this site specifically, or all WVU websites? Search this site Search WVU Toggle Search Home Career Opportunities Why WVU WVU Achievements and Rankings Outdoor Adventure Biking Climbing Hiking Kayaking Rafting Skiing Community Info Dual Career Program Required Notices Home Required Notices Required Notices Clery Act According to federal law, West Virginia University must publish and distribute an\n  Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR) to current students and employees\n  and to give notice of its availability to prospective ones. The ASR includes statistics\n  for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus,\n  in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by West Virginia\n  University, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible\n  from the campus. The ASR also includes institutional policies concerning campus\n  security, such as policies concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the\n  reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a hard copy\n  of the ASR by contacting the W. Va. Univ. Police at 304-293-3136 or by accessing it electronically. Learn More About the Clery Act at WVU Title IX In accordance with Title IX regulations, the University’s Title IX Coordinator contact\n  information is as follows: James Goins Jr., MLS Director of Compliance Title IX Coordinator Office of Compliance and Prevention Education West Virginia University 304-293-5600 office James.goins@mail.wvu.edu Learn More About Title IX at WVU Equal Opportunity West Virginia University is proud to be an Equal Opportunity employer. The University\n    values its faculty, staff, and students, and invites applications from all qualified\n    applicants including veterans and those with disabilities. Equal Opportunity is the Law Poster Equal Opportunity Supplement Poster Pay Transparency Provision Labor Condition Applications West Virginia University sponsors foreign national employees in H-1B and E-3 status,\n    which are statuses reserved for those working in a specialty occupation. For\n    these statuses, West Virginia University is required to obtain a certified Labor\n    Condition Application (LCA) (Form ETA-9035) from the U.S. Department of Labor\n    before it may submit a nonimmigrant petition to U.S. Citizenship and Immigration\n    Services (USCIS). When it files an LCA, West Virginia University attests that it will adhere to certain\n    regulatory requirements associated with the H-1B and E-3 programs. Amongst these\n    requirements is a notice provision, which stipulates that notice must be provided\n    to U.S. workers on the date an LCA is filed (or within the 30-day period before\n    the LCA is filed). The notice must include: The number of nonimmigrants the employer is seeking to employ The occupational classifications in which the nonimmigrant(s) will\n      be employed The wages offered The period of employment The location(s) at which the nonimmigrant(s) will be employed To provide the required notice, West Virginia University has partnered with LaborLess\n      to provide access to the LCAs it has filed for job opportunities which have\n      been filled by H-1B and E-3 candidates. All LCAs filed by West Virginia University\n      are available for public inspection at West Virginia University, International\n      Students and Scholars Services, Purinton House, 1505 University Avenue, Morgantown,\n      WV 26506. Complaints alleging misrepresentation of materials facts and/or failure to comply\n      with the terms of an LCA may be filed using the WH-4 Form with any office of\n      the Wage and Hour Division, Employment Standards Administration, U.S. Department\n      of Labor. A listing of the Wage and Hour Division offices may be obtained at https://www.dol.dog/agencies/whd . For more information and/or questions, please contact International Students\n      and Scholars Services at isss-scholars@mail.wvu.edu . Access LaborLess to See Current Notices Learn More About H-1B and E-3 Specialty Occupations and LCA Notice Requirements Contact Us Talent Acquisition and Recruitment Location : 4 8 Donely Street, 4th Fl, Morgantown, WV  26501 Phone : 304-293-6006 Email : Employment@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Operating Hours 8:15 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Monday - Friday Excluding University holidays Announcements No announcements to show. Accreditations Web Standards Privacy Notice Questions or Comments? © 2026 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on April 8, 2026. A-Z Site Index Campus Map WVU Careers Directory Give Handshake WVU Safety Notification System WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"
    },
